[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2590919748","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101554#issuecomment-2590919748","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101554","id":2590919748,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6abkxE","user":{"login":"TCROC","id":24307049,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzA3MDQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24307049?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC","html_url":"https://github.com/TCROC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-14T19:18:35Z","updated_at":"2025-01-14T19:18:35Z","body":"Also, shout-out to @clayjohn @Calinou and @DarioSamo for all the help debugging and finding a workaround! ♥️","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2590919748/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2590924535","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101554#issuecomment-2590924535","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101554","id":2590924535,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6abl73","user":{"login":"TCROC","id":24307049,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzA3MDQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24307049?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC","html_url":"https://github.com/TCROC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-14T19:21:06Z","updated_at":"2025-01-14T19:21:06Z","body":"And one more thing to note:\n\nI tested a quick POC with @DarioSamo 's suggestion by manually setting:\n\n```cpp\nscene_state.used_screen_texture = true;\nscene_state.used_depth_texture = true;\n```\n\nand can confirm it fixes the stutter.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2590924535/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2619751289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101554#issuecomment-2619751289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101554","id":2619751289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cJjt5","user":{"login":"DarioSamo","id":538504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODUwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioSamo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-28T18:22:58Z","updated_at":"2025-01-28T18:23:34Z","body":"The core of the issue would be that it's possible for elements to trigger the first usage of a feature only when they come into view and not just by the fact they exist in the scene altogether. Following the idea behind Ubershaders, we can likely delegate the detection of this into the surface detection step and set an initial default scene state where the scene is _assumed_ to require these features even if the objects are not visible yet. This would avoid any stutters caused by the sudden creation of the resources that these features need.\n\nThe counters idea seems like the most solid opportunity at achieving this so far. This approach would also allow eliminating the detection of these features from the step where the render list is filled out.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2619751289/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2620067463","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101554#issuecomment-2620067463","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101554","id":2620067463,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cKw6H","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-28T21:13:07Z","updated_at":"2025-01-28T21:13:07Z","body":"> The core of the issue would be that it's possible for elements to trigger the first usage of a feature only when they come into view and not just by the fact they exist in the scene altogether. Following the idea behind Ubershaders, we can likely delegate the detection of this into the surface detection step and set an initial default scene state where the scene is _assumed_ to require these features even if the objects are not visible yet. This would avoid any stutters caused by the sudden creation of the resources that these features need.\n> \n> The counters idea seems like the most solid opportunity at achieving this so far. This approach would also allow eliminating the detection of these features from the step where the render list is filled out.\n\nI think we could even go simpler. The stutter is most likely from allocating the needed buffers. Once allocated, we don't free the buffers unless the screen size changes. Therefore, we don't need to track count we could do something like:\n```\nIf any object in the frame needs refraction\n    ensure buffers are allocated\nRender visible objects in frame\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2620067463/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2620278488","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101554#issuecomment-2620278488","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101554","id":2620278488,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cLkbY","user":{"login":"TCROC","id":24307049,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzA3MDQ5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24307049?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC","html_url":"https://github.com/TCROC","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TCROC/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-28T23:41:47Z","updated_at":"2025-01-28T23:42:08Z","body":"> I think we could even go simpler. The stutter is most likely from allocating the needed buffers. Once allocated, we don't free the buffers unless the screen size changes. Therefore, we don't need to track count we could do something like:\n> \n> ```\n> If any object in the frame needs refraction\n>     ensure buffers are allocated\n> Render visible objects in frame\n> ```\n\nWon't this still have the problem of an initial stutter when they come into frame?  Shouldn't the logic be more like:\n\n \n```\nIf any object in the scene needs refraction\n     ensure buffers are allocated\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2620278488/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794233997","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101554#issuecomment-2794233997","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101554","id":2794233997,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mjKCN","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-10T15:25:52Z","updated_at":"2025-04-10T15:25:52Z","body":"Resolved with godotengine/godot#105175, which doesn't think it's merged for some reason but it definitely is!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794233997/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]